# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — live backend for the Galiyat advisories
# (dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys, or the "Connect" dialog)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmno.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The PUBLISHABLE key (sb_publishable_...) — safe to ship to the browser.
# The legacy "anon public" key (eyJ...) works here too.
# NEVER put the secret key (sb_secret_...) or service_role key in this file.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Staff accounts live in Supabase (Authentication -> Users).
# NOTE (security):
#   - Do NOT add VITE_ADMIN_EMAIL / VITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD or any other
#     credential here: every VITE_ variable is inlined into the public
#     JavaScript bundle at build time and anyone can read it.
#   - Turn OFF "Allow new users to sign up" in Supabase Auth settings, and
#     apply supabase/updates-01-staff-access.sql so only listed staff emails
#     can write advisories.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "Track Your Location" (tourist safety tracking)
# Uses the SAME two Supabase variables above — no extra keys are needed.
#   1. Run supabase/updates-06-tourist-tracking.sql in the SQL editor
#   2. Enable pg_cron (Database -> Extensions) for the auto cleanup jobs
# See docs/tourist-tracking.md for details.
# No Google Maps key is required: the tracking maps use the same free
# OpenStreetMap/Leaflet setup as the existing tourist map page.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
